.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH qdrop 1  "qdrop 0.0.1" 
.SH NAME
qdrop \- Peer\-to\-peer clipboard, file, and link bridge for your own devices.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqdrop\fR [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Peer\-to\-peer clipboard, file, and link bridge for your own devices.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase log verbosity (debug). Overridden by `RUST_LOG`
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress progress/status output (errors still print)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
qdrop\-pair(1)
Pair with another device, or manage existing pairings
.TP
qdrop\-peers(1)
List paired peers and their status
.TP
qdrop\-send(1)
Send one or more files to a peer (use `\-` for stdin)
.TP
qdrop\-recv(1)
Wait for an incoming file; print its path or stream it to stdout
.TP
qdrop\-paste(1)
Print a peer\*(Aqs shared clipboard text to stdout
.TP
qdrop\-copy(1)
Read stdin and set it as the shared clipboard
.TP
qdrop\-open(1)
Open a URL on a peer
.TP
qdrop\-clip(1)
Control clipboard synchronization
.TP
qdrop\-auth(1)
Pre\-authorize a paired peer to send here unattended
.TP
qdrop\-status(1)
Show live daemon status (peers, clipboard)
.TP
qdrop\-doctor(1)
Diagnose why sync isn\*(Aqt working
.TP
qdrop\-daemon(1)
Run the qdrop daemon in the foreground
.TP
qdrop\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.0.1
